  {
   "id": "ty-lock-trade",
   "kind": "trade",
   "headline": "Across Town in the Winter of the Four-Way Trades",
   "body": [
    "The winter after Y82 rearranged the league. Skura left the Jets for Atlanta, and a run of three- and four-team trades moved starters all over the map. Lock ended up with the Giants. The Jets replaced him with Dan Stout, a 79-rated veteran from the Ravens, and the Giants' own quarterback, Drake Wise, went through Atlanta to Baltimore without playing a game for the Falcons.",
    "By the market's reading that winter, New York got the bargain. Lock's card was worth 63, Wise's 869, though Lock had the rings, the MVPs and the better grade, and Wise had no rings at all. It took years for the prices to catch up. Neither quarterback won anything after the deal: Wise played 105 more games and retired a Raven, and Lock played 237 more in a Giants uniform without another ring."
   ],
