  {
   "id": "ty-lock-market",
   "kind": "market",
   "headline": "A Card That Climbed for Thirteen Years Without a Ring",
   "body": [
    "The market came around to Lock slowly and then all at once. His card was worth 63 when he left the Jets and 108 after his first Giants season. It reached 1,110 after Y88 and 2,928 after Y91, and in Y93, a season his touchdown passes fell from 32 to 26, it still rose 30%. After Y94 it passed Wise's for the first time, 5,090 to 5,074, years after Wise had played his last game. It closed at 5,810."
   ],
